# UX copy (Russian)

Applies to any string a user reads: buttons, labels, validation and API error messages,
toasts, empty states, modal text, emails, page metadata. The brand is **Астрология_Инь** -
a personal astrologer selling consultations, with a bonus and referral program.

## Language and register

- All user-facing text is **Russian**. English is only for code, logs and developer
  comments. Fix English leftovers when you touch them (`Loading...`, `Delete`,
  `Recent Users`, `Phone number`, `"Reset password link"` subject, `timeAgo` output).
- Default register is **«вы»** (lowercase, as the codebase mostly does: «Вы можете
  просмотреть...»). Do not mix «ты» and «вы» on one screen - several components do
  (`BonusList`: «Ты заработал» next to «Вы заработали»); when you touch such a component,
  align it to «вы». Switch the whole product to «ты» only if the developer asks.
- Keep `<html lang>` aligned with the content (`ru`) when you touch `app/layout.tsx`.
- Use «ё» and the typographic quotes «» consistently with the surrounding file; normal
  Russian typography (including the em dash) is fine inside UI strings.

## Where copy lives

- Validation, payment-status and location messages: `app/constants/messages.json`
  (`messages.validation.required`, `messages.payments[status]`). New reusable messages
  go there; new keys are camelCase.
- Screen copy is inline in JSX (the house pattern). Keep it in the component, not in a
  new i18n layer - there is no i18n library and none is planned.
- Brand name comes from `app/constants/brand.tsx` (`BRAND_NAME` / `BRAND_NAME_STRING`),
  never typed by hand.
- API error messages are set in services/handlers (`ApiError.badRequest("...")`) and shown
  verbatim by the client - write them for the user, not for the developer.

## Tone

- **Precise, warm, not mystical-spam.** Describe what the consultation gives and what the
  user does next; no "судьба изменится навсегда" style promises, no guaranteed outcomes.
- **No pressure around money or bonuses.** Explain the rule («20% стоимости можно оплатить
  бонусами»), do not shame or rush («только сегодня», «успейте»).
- **Clarity first**: the user never wonders what happens next. After payment: what we
  check, how long, where to look (`messages.payments.CHECKING` is the model).
- **Buttons name the action**: «Войти», «Зарегистрироваться», «Оплатить», «Скопировать
  номер» - not «Отправить»/«ОК».
- **Errors explain how to fix**: «Пожалуйста введите корректный адрес электронной почты»,
  not «Ошибка». Server failures: say that something went wrong and what to try
  («Попробуйте ещё раз или напишите мне в Telegram»).
- **Write it, then cut it in half.**

## Amounts, prices, dates

- Never type a price, bonus amount or percentage into copy. Read it from the data
  (consultation `price` + `Currency` from `prisma/enumAdapter.ts`) or the constants in
  `app/constants/constants.ts` (`REGISTRATION_BONUS`, `PERCENTAGE_TO_PAY_BY_BONUS`).
- Dates through `formatDate` from `utils/formatting.ts` (locale `ru`); bonus plurals through
  the existing pluralisation helper (`балл / балла / баллов`).

## Before / after

```
❌ "Ошибка."                      ✅ "Не удалось сохранить изменения. Попробуйте ещё раз."
❌ "Submit"                       ✅ "Оплатить консультацию"
❌ "Loading..."                   ✅ "Загружаем..." (or a skeleton, no text)
❌ "Ты заработал 3000 баллов"     ✅ "Вы заработали 3000 баллов" (amount from data)
❌ "Воити в аккаунт"              ✅ "Войти в аккаунт"
```

## Gotcha

A grammatically fine string can still be off-voice (cold, pushy, or vague). Read it aloud as
if explaining to a friend who is paying for a consultation for the first time.
